* About this document

This document should be used to help to configure *any* Ubuntu distro to working-distro with the most common set-up that I'm used to. Main tools and look&feel from preconfigured repo.

The structure that I want is a private repository that will have all the scripts needed to config the new distro.

This entire file is a literate document so once you installed Emacs and Spacemacs you will be able to execute the configurations as you wish.

Summarizing, the first step is to have git.

#+begin_src sh

sudo apt-get install git

#+end_src

Keep reading!

* Productivity Tools

** Main tool EMACS

The main tool that I'm using since 2018 for Instant Project Management is Emacs, which is mostly the key for many features and tricks that I'm doing in my everyday work stream.

https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/

#+begin_src sh

sudo apt-get install emacs

#+end_src

And the flavour that I like most is the *spacemacs* https://www.spacemacs.org/

#+begin_src sh

git clone https://github.com/syl20bnr/spacemacs ~/.emacs.d

#+end_src

* Terminal tune-up

Powerline is a very usefull aplication when you use git, I recommend to install it.

#+begin_src sh

sudo apt-get install powerline

#+end_src

